He was so lost in thoughts, he didn't hear the shift in the fight inside, and right next to Nine, the wall was hit from the inside. That part collapsed, and an adult, wolf-like creature fell out while wrestling with... something small??? It looked like a fur ball, viciously biting and scratching him up. Another adult, a raccoon came running out, grabbed the small furball, and threw it away - at Nine's direction, who was too stunned to move so far, and the raccoon did not see him until it was too late. Nine collided with the thing, and fell on his back. He shook his head, and quickly looked up to see a badly beaten kid laying on his chest, heaving with some blood trickling down on their cheek and from their nose. Nine looked at their back, and - oh hell nah. It was of course a hedgehog kid, with brown quills and body, their cheeks a light shade of cream yellow, which was probably the colour of their tummy too. Their paws weren't covered with anything, and they only wore some oversized old pants, and a pullover that was clearly too big for them. And when the kid opened their eyes and met with Nine's, suddenly, Nine thought he was looking at that damned blue hedgehog. Same shining, emerald green eyes. "Hey you!" Nine looked up while the kid scrambled down from his chest and hid behind him. The raccoon spoke, while his wolf friend was hissing from getting his entire arm bit in several places, each one bleeding freely. His left cheek also had some quills stuck in it.
